@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@
+name: Yuedu Source-only Reader Measurements and UMD Parser
+
+on:
+  push:
+    tags:
+      - 'reader-measurements-*'
+
+permissions:
+  contents: read
+
+concurrency:
+  group: reader-measurements-${{ github.ref }}
+  cancel-in-progress: false
+
+defaults:
+  run:
+    shell: bash
+
+jobs:
+  measurements:
+    runs-on: macos-15
+    timeout-minutes: 80
+    steps:
+      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7.0.1
+        with:
+          persist-credentials: false
+      - uses: actions/setup-python@5fda3b95a4ea91299a34e894583c3862153e4b97 # v7.0.0
+        with:
+          python-version: '3.12'
+      - name: Verify exact source tag and portable evidence guards
+        run: |
+          mkdir -p .build/ci-logs
+          python -B scripts/reader-experience/smoke-tools.py validate-tag --tag-prefix reader-measurements-
+          python -B scripts/reader-experience/test-smoke-tools.py -v 2>&1 | tee .build/ci-logs/shared-smoke-tools.log
+          python -B scripts/reader-experience/test-reader-stage-baseline.py -v 2>&1 | tee .build/ci-logs/shared-stage-tools.log
+          python -B scripts/reader-experience/test-reader-launch-memory.py -v 2>&1 | tee .build/ci-logs/measurement-shapes.log
+          python -B scripts/reader-experience/test-collect-reader-measurements.py -v 2>&1 | tee .build/ci-logs/measurement-binding-tools.log
+          python -B scripts/reader-experience/test-umd-fixtures.py -v 2>&1 | tee .build/ci-logs/umd-fixture-tools.log
+          python -B scripts/reader-experience/inspect-umd-fixtures.py --root 'Tests/iOS/yuedu appTests/Fixtures/UMD' > .build/ci-logs/umd-fixture-integrity.json
+          bash -n scripts/reader-experience/reader-measurements.sh
+      - name: Select the installed toolchain and Simulator
+        run: |
+          export DEVELOPER_DIR="$(bash scripts/sim.sh xcode)"
+          export YUEDU_DEST="$(bash scripts/sim.sh dest)"
+          echo "DEVELOPER_DIR=$DEVELOPER_DIR" >> "$GITHUB_ENV"
+          echo "YUEDU_DEST=$YUEDU_DEST" >> "$GITHUB_ENV"
+          xcodebuild -version > .build/ci-logs/measurement-xcode.log
+      - name: Run three independent selections and retain every group before gating
+        timeout-minutes: 70
+        env:
+          LEGADO_RUNTIME_SOURCE_ONLY: '1'
+        run: bash scripts/reader-experience/reader-measurements.sh > .build/ci-logs/reader-measurements-runner.log 2>&1
+      - name: Preserve original artifacts and all failure evidence
+        if: always()
+        uses: actions/upload-artifact@cf430e030ddbb5b0abf93d22962f4752f3646cd9 # v7.0.2
+        with:
+          name: reader-measurements-evidence
+          path: |
+            .build/ci-logs
+            .build/reader-measurements
+          if-no-files-found: error
+          retention-days: 14
+      - name: Record the observation boundary
+        if: always()
+        run: |
+          cat >> "$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY" <<'TEXT'
+          This independent source-only checkpoint selects memory 1 method/1 execution, launch UI 1/1, and pure UMD parser 11/11, each with zero failures/skips/expected failures and its own original log, xcresult, summary, tests tree, source/environment binding and count result. A recoverable group failure does not prevent collecting the others; the combined gate still fails.
+
+          Launch requires five fresh-process observations to the current CPU layer submission plus a visible AX UTF16/text anchor; import/setup is outside the interval and automation navigation remains included. Memory requires two owned fixtures times five samples, thirty raw phases each, same-snapshot TASK_VM_INFO footprint/RSS, actual periodic gaps and no failed/on-main kernel queries. The imported shape collector alone never attests execution. UMD selects only the isolated text decoder/file parser against five owned original-Java goldens; it does not enable product import or MOBI/cover/DRM.
+
+          The old TXT one-method selection and fifty-row stage protocol are unchanged and are not run here. This is Debug Simulator evidence only when the actual new passing XCTest identities, committed source, overlay and SDK/runtime artifacts validate. It is not device-cold startup, GPU presentation, an exact kernel peak, a production speedup or physical-device acceptance.
+          TEXT
